Kaioh the Tracker was given to [[Den Fears]] by [[Teeg]] after Teeg related to Den's experience of being completely new to the world of Seekers. This was followed by a training session about Kaioh's tracking abilities. Den later invoked him in [[Hernán Cortés]]'s vault to fight against [[the Organization]]. Kaioh tried to locate the [[Ring]] of [[Umbra]] the Shadow Jaguar but was hit by an attack from [[Shadow Agent]]. After being protected from further attacks by [[Sophie Casterwill]]'s [[Enfluxion]], Kaioh was able to point at the Umbra's Ring which [[Dante Vale]] immediately grabbed. After being cornered by [[Conquistador]], Kaioh attempted to stop him but was defeated and sent back to his Amulet. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}

Den invoked Kaioh in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]] to fight against [[Harrison Fears]]'s newly [[Antedeluvian|Powerbonded Antedeluvian]] but was defeated by the Titan's 'Lifedrain' ability. Antedeluvian was then able to gain Kaioh's 'Totem Staff'. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

Kaioh was invoked alongside [[Tersly]]'s [[Red Searcher]] to find the [[Lodestone]]. Den commented that Kaioh would find it quicker, however both Titans were sent back to their Amulets by the Lodestone's Anti-Magic field. {{source|The Dead Magic Island}}

In the magical floating castle of [[Tír na nÓg]], Kaioh fought against numerous [[Dullahan]] and [[Firbolg]] Titans. Despite defeating a large number of them, Kaioh was sent back to his Amulet by [[Firbolg]]. {{source|Back Home}}
